    "result_text": "The only runnable test is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are `AcceptanceBase` and a package artifact), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on the `POST /api/owners` create pipeline \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same `firstName` and `lastName`, case-insensitively \u2014 and exposed it on the owner representation.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New function step** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/CountNamesakes.java`: iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()` and counts owners matching the new owner's first and last name via `equalsIgnoreCase`, then calls `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so `findAll()` sees only the pre-existing owners (\"before this create\").\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `countNamesakes` step (governed by `transaction`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added a nullable `Integer namesakeCount` mapped to a new `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it straight through to/from the DTO by name (same pattern as `customerCode`), so it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `namesake_count INTEGER` to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files, and appended the trailing `NULL` to the positional owner INSERTs in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the profile the tests use; h2/mysql/postgres either use named-column inserts or have no seed owners).\n\n5. **OpenAPI** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer field to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCountsNamesakes` (creates two \"Ann <surname>\" owners and expects `$.namesakeCount == 1` on the second) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
